WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.064 --> 00:00:00.897
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.897 --> 00:00:03.200
- Please welcome one of
my favorite actresses

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.996
on planet Earth and
history, Elisabeth Moss.

00:00:05.996 --> 00:00:07.241
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.241 --> 00:00:09.622
(upbeat bright music)

00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:10.455
- Hi.

00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:17.795
This is for you.

00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:20.362
I know you're all about your
suits, and you look so cute.

00:00:20.362 --> 00:00:21.384
So I had to.

00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:22.217
- I do.

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.815
So beautiful.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:24.648
Look.

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:27.873
(Kate laughs)

00:00:27.873 --> 00:00:29.080
- It's so good to see you.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.562
- Oh my god, I'm so happy to
see you, I can't believe it.

00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:34.300
- It's been way too long.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.430
- It has been way too long.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.715
And this is the dream.

00:00:36.715 --> 00:00:38.245
We're hear in person.

00:00:38.245 --> 00:00:40.620
IRL, as the kids say.
- In person.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.851
Yes.

00:00:41.851 --> 00:00:42.684
IRL.

00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:44.100
- Are you comfortable?
- I think so.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.081
- Is the pillow good?

00:00:45.081 --> 00:00:47.100
- (laughs) I'm good.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.830
Drew Barrymore just fluffed my pillow.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:52.168
- I will fluff your pillow
until the end of time.

00:00:52.168 --> 00:00:53.001
(Kate laughs)

00:00:53.001 --> 00:00:56.000
All right, so, you are in...

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.470
is it true that you're
in season five right now

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.303
of "The Handmaid's Tale"?

00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:00.585
- Yes, yes.
- Right now, right now!

00:01:00.585 --> 00:01:02.115
(Drew screams)

00:01:02.115 --> 00:01:04.236
(audience applauds)

00:01:04.236 --> 00:01:06.940
And I love where it's going.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.730
Ugh, there's just, we are all human.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.950
And when people have been
wronged, we want to make it right.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:13.783
- Yes. (chuckles)

00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:16.940
- And it's just delicious and bitey

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.530
and fighty and everything.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.420
What's going on?

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:20.253
How's the season going?

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:21.460
Any spoilers?

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.293
How's it going?

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.110
- It's going really well.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:25.992
We're halfway through.
- Uh-huh.

00:01:25.992 --> 00:01:26.825
- Uh-huh.

00:01:26.825 --> 00:01:27.740
She's already excited,
I haven't said anything,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.220
you're already excited.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.100
- My favorite show ever.
- I know, thank you.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.010
I will say that it's a very big season.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.320
We've been on location a lot.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.160
We've been in the studio very little,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.260
which for us means that it's very big.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.810
And we're just constantly on the road.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.410
A lot of locations.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.930
June's journey is big.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.540
The other characters'
journeys are very big

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.463
and June's dealing with,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.723
what does freedom actually mean?

00:01:58.843 --> 00:02:00.980
And can she really be free?

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.090
And what does that mean?

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.890
And where do I place my anger?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.233
And these really big questions

00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:08.620
that I think are also really identifiable.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:12.200
- Yes, it's so true.
- Yeah.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.070
- Whoa.
- Yeah.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.378
- Oh.

00:02:15.378 --> 00:02:17.900
(Kate laughs)

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.430
Okay, well, in your new project

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.840
which is another example
of your immaculate work

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.140
and performance and style.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.630
It's quintessential.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:31.247
If you love Elisabeth
Moss, this show is for you.

00:02:31.247 --> 00:02:32.667
"Shining Girls."

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.370
Tell us about that show.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.890
- Yes, it's very, very
twisty, very twisty.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.610
It's one of those shows
that the first episode

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:40.820
you think what you know

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.300
and then the second episode, you're like,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.910
oh no, it's completely different.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.980
And then the third and fourth
and so on and so forth.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.570
So I play Kirby who works
at the Chicago Sun-Times,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.190
she's an archivist in 1992.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.740
Which was really fun.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:59.160
And she had survived a brutal
assault six years prior

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.620
to when our show begins.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.200
So that's like one side of the show.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.730
And then there's another side of the show

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.130
which is she's dealing with
an ever-shifting reality.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.980
And I mean quite literally.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.400
Like things change around
her and she doesn't know why.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.400
So the show is actually about
her figuring out how and why.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.290
- And there's things that match up

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.940
to things that happen
that give her revelations.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.090
And it goes on a ride from
there and it is so good.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.470
It is a rollercoaster ride.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.875
- Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:34.042
(upbeat bright music)

